== Notes
1. No gate failed. No fixes were needed and the clone stayed clean.
2. Coverage. core-test printed "lines with all attached points covered: 54.00% (3730/6843)". The difference from the
   31a1568 gate comes from step order, not from the RTL. In this chain `make test` ran before core-test, and its six
   crypto KAT testbenches (cov_sha256, cov_sha512, cov_keccak, cov_ecfield, cov_cryptotop, cov_hashstream) left
   coverage files that the core-test merge picks up (`ls build/sim/cov_*.dat`). The earlier gates ran `make test` after
   core-test. Merged without those six files and annotated from sim/, the figure is 55.00% (3494/6255), the same as
   the 31a1568 gate. The coverage .dat files (20 GB) were deleted after the run; the logs stay in
   ~/relgate73f/{sigil,boot}/build/gates/ on sigil-fpga-build.
3. The 5.020 lint used the wrapper fixed in the first release gate (note 1 of linux-release-73-gates-2026-10-22.log);
   it ran first time.
4. The staged evidence tarball (20:07 UTC) predates this log. stage_release73.sh picks up
   linux-release-73-*-2026-10-22.log, so this file is included only after the assets are restaged.

